================================================================================================
(I) DIM-2 NO-GO: det formula verified on random instances, then the 4-line proof
================================================================================================
  trial 0 (k=4, degA=0, degh=3): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 1 (k=1, degA=3, degh=3): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 2 (k=4, degA=0, degh=1): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 3 (k=3, degA=0, degh=3): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 4 (k=2, degA=3, degh=0): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 5 (k=2, degA=3, degh=2): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 6 (k=1, degA=2, degh=2): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  trial 7 (k=4, degA=0, degh=2): det == -[Ah + s(kAh'+A'h)] : True
  PROOF (4 lines): Keller => Ah + s(kAh'+A'h) = c const; leading coeff of the
  LHS at degree a+b is (1 + a + k*b) A_a h_b != 0 for (a,b) != (0,0); so a=b=0,
  F = (c1 y, c2 x): LINEAR.  The equivariant mechanism CANNOT produce a JC_2
  counterexample.  QED (in-class).

